<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table"><span id="A1.T7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Table 7</span>. </span><span id="A1.T7.6" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Statistical details of <span id="A1.T7.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">M4DocBench</span> by domains and </span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F4" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F4.sf1" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.sf1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a)</span> </span><span id="A1.F4.sf1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The question requires integrating textual and tabular evidence from multiple market analysis reports to compare fund-raising and exit-return proportions across different months. The reasoning involves multi-hop retrieval and numerical computation across documents. </span></figcaption><img src="2510.21603v1/data_display1.png" id="A1.F4.sf1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/120;" width="471" height="120" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1">
<figure id="A1.F4.sf2" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel ltx_align_center">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.sf2.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(b)</span> </span><span id="A1.F4.sf2.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">This example illustrates a cross-document, cross-modal, multi-hop reasoning task. The model needs to extract and compare structured program information across multiple brochures to determine the shortest graduation time under the given limitation. </span></figcaption><img src="2510.21603v1/data_display2.png" id="A1.F4.sf2.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/100;" width="471" height="100" alt="Refer to caption">
</figure></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F4.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 4</span>. </span><span id="A1.F4.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Demonstration of two typical annotations of <span id="A1.F4.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">M4DocBench</span>. Note that they are simplified for brevity.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F5" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.21603v1/layout_chunk.png" id="A1.F5.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/171;" width="471" height="171" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F5.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 5</span>. </span><span id="A1.F5.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">The overview of layout-aware chunking process and multimodal-to-text transcription.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F6" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21603v1/radar_chart_e2e.svg" id="A1.F6.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/187;" width="471" height="187"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F6.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 6</span>. </span><span id="A1.F6.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Accuracy and retrieval performance of <span id="A1.F6.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Doc-Researcher</span> using different backbone LLMs and retrieval schemes.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
<figure id="A1.F7" class="ltx_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_figure">
<div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21603v1/radar_chart_ret_domain.svg" id="A1.F7.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/163;" width="471" height="163"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21603v1/radar_mmdocir.svg" id="A1.F7.g2" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:429/135;" width="429" height="135"></object></div><div class="ltx_flex_break"></div><div class="ltx_flex_cell ltx_flex_size_1"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2510.21603v1/radar_mmdocir_p2.svg" id="A1.F7.g3" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_figure_panel ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:471/161;" width="471" height="161"></object></div></div>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="A1.F7.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 7</span>. </span><span id="A1.F7.5" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">(a) Retrieval performance (break-down by 4 domains) using text/vision/hybrid scheme on <span id="A1.F7.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">M4DocBench</span>. (b) Retrieval performance (break-down by 10 domains) using text/vision/hybrid scheme on MMDocIR. Note that recall of layout is not applicable to vision-only scheme, as the retrieval is at page level. MMDocIR focuses on single-document VQA, hence document recall is not applicable.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="A2" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix B </span>Implementation Details</h2>

<div id="A2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Multimodal Document Parsing</span>. We utilize MinerU v2.0.6 for document parsing. The chunking strategy segments text when: (1) length exceeds 300 tokens, (2) page boundaries are crossed, or (3) section headers are encountered. Images and tables are extracted as independent units. <span id="A2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Image Processing</span>: Visual content was processed using <a href="https://huggingface.co/Qwen/Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct</a><span id="footnote4" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">4</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">4</span>
            
            
            
          Qwen2.5-VL-7B-Instruct is served using <a href="https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_href">vLLM</a> for efficient and stable inference.</span></span></span> for description generation. Visual chunks of image size less than 10KB are excluded. This is to filter decorative icons and insignificant graphics, as well as relieving computational overhead. <span id="A2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">OCR Processing</span>: PDF pages were converted using PyMuPDF (fitz) and subjected to Tesseract OCR with a chunk size of 140 characters for structured text extraction.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p2" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Multimodal Indexing and Data Persistence</span>.
We deploy <span id="A2.p2.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">MySQL database</span> to store document metadata, including document summaries, structured full-text, chunks (both text and cropped images), pages (both text and screenshots), and layout bounding boxes (bbox coordinates).
We summarize the checkpoints for retriever deployments in Table <a href="#A1.T6" title="Table 6 ‣ Appendix A M4DocBench: Supplementary Materials ‣ Doc-Researcher: A Unified System for Multimodal Document Parsing and Deep Research" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>. Retrievers are used to convert passages of different modalities and granularities into vector representations.
We deploy <span id="A2.p2.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Milvus vector database</span> to maintain dense vectors for textual and visual chunks, and page screenshots. Document names serve as filtering conditions for retrieval operations. For <span id="A2.p2.1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">multi-vector storage</span>, we save them locally as np.savez_compressed, with each document stored as an individual NPZ file for efficient retrieval.</p>
</div>
<div id="A2.p3" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A2.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A2.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold ltx_font_italic">Deep Research Framework</span>.
We implement <span id="A2.p3.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Doc-Researcher</span>, the multi-agent deep research workflow using LangGraph<span id="footnote5" class="ltx_note ltx_role_footnote"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup><span class="ltx_note_outer"><span class="ltx_note_content"><sup class="ltx_note_mark">5</sup>
            <span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_note">5</span>
            
            
            
          <a href="https://www.langchain.com/langgraph" title="" class="ltx_ref ltx_url ltx_font_typewriter">https://www.langchain.com/langgraph</a></span></span></span>.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="A3" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix C </span>Extended Experimental Results</h2>

<div id="A3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A3.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#A1.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Appendix A M4DocBench: Supplementary Materials ‣ Doc-Researcher: A Unified System for Multimodal Document Parsing and Deep Research" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a> depicts the accuracy and performance of <span id="A3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">Doc-Researcher</span> according to different domains and granularities.
Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A M4DocBench: Supplementary Materials ‣ Doc-Researcher: A Unified System for Multimodal Document Parsing and Deep Research" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>a depicts the retrieval performance on <span id="A3.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">M4DocBench</span> by 4 different domains and 3 different top-<math id="A3.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> settings.
Figure <a href="#A1.F7" title="Figure 7 ‣ Appendix A M4DocBench: Supplementary Materials ‣ Doc-Researcher: A Unified System for Multimodal Document Parsing and Deep Research" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>b depicts the retrieval performance on MMDocIR by 10 different domains and 3 different top-<math id="A3.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="k" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>k</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">k</annotation></semantics></math> settings. This is extended retrieval results of Table <a href="#S5.T2" title="Table 2 ‣ 5. Experiment ‣ Doc-Researcher: A Unified System for Multimodal Document Parsing and Deep Research" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
</section>
</article>
